Detect the caught-mon Pokédex page independently of its borrowed battle VBlank.
The port bridge selects CTR_CENTRED_POKEDEX_CAUGHT, not the field Pokédex:
fixed BG2/BG3 scroll, a bounded 240x160 picture and stripe-only margins on
the whole bottom screen. Keep this task hook through preparation and exit;
do not register the borrowed callback as a Pokédex callback.
Applies after 0053-accelerated-berry-clock.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

diff --git a/src/pokedex.c b/src/pokedex.c
--- a/src/pokedex.c
+++ b/src/pokedex.c
@@ -5814,6 +5814,16 @@ IntrCallback CtrPokedex_VBlankCallback(void)
     return VBlankCB_Pokedex;
 }
-
+
+bool8 CtrPokedex_IsCaughtMonPage(void)
+{
+    u8 taskId = FindTaskIdByFunc(Task_DisplayCaughtMonDexPage);
+
+    return (taskId != TASK_NONE && gTasks[taskId].data[0] != 0)
+        || FuncIsActiveTask(Task_HandleCaughtMonPageInput)
+        || FuncIsActiveTask(Task_ExitCaughtMonPage);
+}
+
+
 bool8 CtrPokedex_IsOpen(void)
 {
     return sPokedexView != NULL && (gMain.callback2 == CB2_Pokedex || gMain.callback2 == CB2_OpenPokedex);
